@startuml opensky-rate-limit-lifecycle
title OpenSky poller: rate-limit lifecycle (planNextPoll)

hide empty description
skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

state POLLING : next request after the interval
state PAUSED : one timer, no requests while waiting

[*] --> POLLING : startup, first request immediately

POLLING --> POLLING : 200 (logs credits_remaining)\nor network error / 5xx / Kafka failure
POLLING --> PAUSED : 429\nlog "pausing requests" once

PAUSED --> PAUSED : 429 again\nlog "pause extended"
PAUSED --> PAUSED : network error / 5xx / Kafka failure\nno log, nothing reset
PAUSED --> POLLING : 200\nlog "resumed" once\nreset fallback count

note bottom of PAUSED
  How long to wait after a 429
  valid retry header: the longer of the header and the interval
  no usable header: 60 s floor, doubling ceiling, 15 min cap, jitter
  only a 200 resets the fallback count
end note

@enduml
